.TH DVBTX 1 2026-11-02 "dvbtx 0.1.0" "dvbtx manual"
.SH NAME
dvbtx \- DVB transmitter on software radios: live streams, captures and files to DVB-T, DVB-T2, DVB-C, DVB-S, DVB-S2
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY dvbtx
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.YS
.SY dvbtx
.B run
.RB [ \-c
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-s
.IR KEY = VALUE ]...\&
.RI [ "quick setup options" ]
.RI [ "run options" ]
.YS
.SY dvbtx
.B check
|
.B engine\-ini
|
.B epg
.RB [ \-c
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-s
.IR KEY = VALUE ]...\&
.YS
.SY dvbtx
.B channel
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.RI [ ARGS ]
.YS
.SY dvbtx
.B calc
.I STANDARD
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.YS
.SY dvbtx
.B devices
|
.B gpu
.RB [ list | learn ]
.YS
.SY dvbtx
.B make\-backup
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.YS
.SY dvbtx
.B power
.BR save | transmit | default | status | hook
.YS
.SY dvbtx
.BR help " [" \fICOMMAND\fR "] | " \-h " | " \-\-version
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dvbtx
builds complete DVB multiplexes from live streams (HLS, RTMP, SRT, RTSP, Twitch, YouTube, M3U
playlists, tvheadend), capture devices (webcam, HDMI capture, screen), files and pipes, and
modulates them on software radios: HackRF One, USRP B200/B210 (UHD) and any SoapySDR transmitter.
A radio carries any number of carriers (multiplexes) in DVB-T, DVB-T2, DVB-C, DVB-S or DVB-S2;
there can be any number of radios and of services per multiplex.
It generates the PSI/SI tables (PAT, PMT, NIT with logical channel numbers, SDT, EIT from XMLTV,
TDT/TOT), clocks every multiplex on its radio, switches a service to a backup clip when its
source fails, and serves a monitoring and control web page.
.PP
Everything is described in one TOML file,
.BR dvbtx.toml (5),
or for a single radio and carrier on the command line.
How the parts fit together is explained in
.BR dvbtx (7).
.PP
.B Closed coax only.
Radiating on broadcast frequencies is forbidden: dvbtx is meant for a private coaxial network or a
cable to the TV set, with attenuators.
.PP
Without a command,
.B run
is meant:
.B dvbtx \-c my.toml
is
.BR "dvbtx run \-c my.toml" .
.B dvbtx \-h
lists the commands,
.BI "dvbtx " COMMAND " \-h"
or
.BI "dvbtx help " COMMAND
gives the options of one.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Run the transmitter until stopped: the source processes, the C engine
.RB ( dvbtx\-engine (8)),
the SI tables and EPG, the alerts and the web page
.RB ( dvbtx\-web (7)).
SIGINT or SIGTERM stops it; SIGHUP re-reads the EPG folder and the channels of the
configuration file (applied channel by channel, the others untouched).
Needs the rights to open the radios and to take real-time priorities (root, or the systemd
service).
.TP
.B check
Validate the configuration and print the plan: radios with their local oscillator and sample
rate, carriers with their useful bit rate, services with their service_id, logical channel
number and PIDs.
Nothing is transmitted.
.TP
.B channel
List, add, remove, rename, renumber the channels of the running transmitter or change their
source, without touching the others; written back to the configuration file.
See
.BR dvbtx\-channel (1).
.TP
.B calc
Useful MPEG-TS bit rate of a carrier (see
.B CALC OPTIONS
below).
.TP
\fBdevices\fR [\fB\-\-save\fR \fIRADIO\fR [\fB\-\-serial\fR \fIS\fR]]
Ask
.BR hackrf_info ,
.B uhd_find_devices
and
.B SoapySDRUtil
for the radios plugged in and print their
.B driver
and
.BR serial ,
with the radio of the configuration bound to each.
.B \-\-save
.I RADIO
writes in the file the
.B serial
of the device of that radio's driver that no other radio is bound to (a radio without serial
holds the first device of its driver), so that two devices of the same driver no longer swap
after a restart or a replug;
.B \-\-serial
picks one when several are free.
The running transmitter takes it at the next
.B Apply
of the web page or the next start.
.TP
.BR gpu " [" list | learn ]
List the graphics adapters and, for each one and each codec (H.264, HEVC, MPEG-2), the fastest
working way to transcode with it, as learnt (VAAPI, QSV, NVENC; whole chain on the GPU, or only the
encoding).
.B learn
tests every way again now; otherwise
.B dvbtx run
does it in the background when the adapters, their drivers or ffmpeg change.
.TP
.B epg
Load the EPG (files of
.BR epg.dir ,
XMLTV or TSDuck EIT XML, and
.BR epg.urls )
and show for each service the number of events and what is on now and next.
.TP
.B make\-backup
Create the looping clip a service plays while its source is down (see
.B MAKE-BACKUP OPTIONS
below).
.TP
.B power
Power profiles of the whole machine, for a transmitter on battery: every saving while nothing is
on air, a transmit profile while dvbtx runs.
See
.BR dvbtx\-power (8).
.TP
.B engine\-ini
Write the INI file
.B dvbtx run
gives the engine, with its SI tables, and print its path
.RB ( \-o
.I FILE
to choose it).
.TP
.BR help " [" \fICOMMAND " [" \fISUBCOMMAND ]]
The help of a command, as
.BR \-h .
.SH CONFIGURATION OPTIONS
Common to
.BR run ,
.BR check ,
.B engine\-ini
and
.BR epg .
.TP
.BI \-c " FILE" "\fR, \fP\-\-config " FILE
TOML configuration file.
Default
.I /etc/dvbtx/dvbtx.toml
when it exists and no service or frequency is given on the command line.
.TP
.BI \-s " KEY" = VALUE "\fR, \fP\-\-set " KEY = VALUE
Override any setting, repeatable.
Lists are indexed by number:
.BR radio.0.gain=40 ,
.BR carrier.1.frequency=498MHz ,
.BR carrier.0.service.2.source=/srv/clip.ts ,
.BR web.listen=0.0.0.0:8080 .
Values are read as TOML (numbers, booleans, arrays, strings), and
.BR k ,
.BR M ,
.B G
suffixes are accepted
.RB ( 482MHz ,
.BR 6.9M ).
.SS Quick setup
One radio and one carrier, without a file or on top of the first radio and carrier of the file.
.TP
.BI \-\-driver " DRIVER"
.BR hackrf ,
.BR uhd ,
.B soapy
or
.B null
(no radio: the samples are thrown away, for tests).
.TP
.BI \-\-args " ARGS"
Radio arguments, e.g.
.BR serial=0000000000000000a06063c8234e6c5f .
.TP
.BI \-\-gain " DB"
Transmit gain.
.TP
.B \-\-amp
HackRF RF amplifier on.
.TP
.BI \-\-rate " RATE" "\fR, \fP\-\-center " FREQ
Radio sample rate and local oscillator; computed from the carriers by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-standard " STD"
.B dvbt
(default),
.BR dvbt2 ,
.BR dvbc ,
.BR dvbs ,
.B dvbs2
or
.B ts
(no modulation: the multiplex is sent to
.BR carrier.output ).
.TP
.BI \-\-frequency " FREQ" "\fR, \fP\-\-channel " N
Carrier frequency
.RB ( 482MHz ),
or UHF (21\(en69) / VHF (5\(en12) channel number.
.TP
.BI \-\-bandwidth " BW" "\fR, \fP\-\-mode " 2k | 8k "\fR, \fP\-\-constellation " C "\fR, \fP\-\-code\-rate " R "\fR, \fP\-\-guard " G
DVB-T modulation: default 8 MHz, 8k, 64-QAM, 7/8, 1/32.
.TP
.BI \-\-tsid " N"
transport_stream_id.
.TP
.BI \-\-service " NAME" = SOURCE\fR[\fP, KEY = VALUE\fR...]
Add a service, repeatable:
.BR "\-\-service \(dqMovie=/srv/movie.mkv,lcn=2\(dq" .
The source syntax is in
.BR dvbtx\-sources (7).
.SS Run options
.TP
.BI \-\-work\-dir " DIR"
Runtime directory: engine.ini, SI tables (default
.IR /run/dvbtx ).
.TP
.BI \-\-web " HOST" : PORT \fR|\fP none
Address of the web page (default
.BR 127.0.0.1:8080 ),
or none.
.TP
.BI \-\-epg\-dir " DIR"
Folder of XMLTV or TSDuck EIT XML files.
.TP
.BI \-\-analysis\-export " URL"
Send the TSDuck analysis of every multiplex (JSON) to
.BI udp:// host : port
or
.BI tcp:// host : port\fR,
repeatable; turns TSDuck on.
.TP
.BI \-\-stats\-export " URL"
Send the engine statistics and the alerts (JSON, every second) to
.B udp://
or
.BR tcp:// ,
repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tsduck
Do not run the TSDuck analysers.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Debug messages.
.SH CALC OPTIONS
.B dvbtx calc
.BR dvbt | dvbt2 | dvbc | dvbs | dvbs2
prints the useful MPEG-TS bit rate, PSI/SI included.
.TP
.BI \-\-bandwidth " BW"
DVB-T and DVB-T2 channel width (default 8MHz).
.TP
.BR \-\-mode " 2k|8k"
DVB-T (default 8k).
.TP
.BI \-\-constellation " C"
DVB-T: qpsk, 16qam, 64qam; DVB-T2 up to 256qam; DVB-C: 16qam to 256qam.
.TP
.BI \-\-modulation " M"
DVB-S2: qpsk, 8psk, 16apsk, 32apsk; DVB-S2X also 64apsk, 128apsk, 256apsk.
.TP
.BI \-\-code\-rate " R" "\fR, \fP\-\-guard " G
Code rate and guard interval.
.TP
.BI \-\-symbol\-rate " S"
DVB-C, DVB-S, DVB-S2 (e.g. 27.5M).
.TP
.BI \-\-fft " N" "\fR, \fP\-\-extended " yes | no "\fR, \fP\-\-pilot " PP N
DVB-T2: FFT size (1k to 32k), extended carriers, pilot pattern.
.TP
.BR \-\-frame " normal|short" ", " \-\-no\-pilots
DVB-S2 (and DVB-T2) FEC frame; DVB-S2 without pilots.
.TP
.BI \-\-services " N"
Also the share of each of N services (3 % kept for PSI/SI).
.TP
.B \-\-table
DVB-T: every constellation, code rate and guard interval.
.SH MAKE-BACKUP OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " FILE"
Default
.IR /var/lib/dvbtx/backup.ts .
.TP
.BI \-\-text " TEXT" "\fR, \fP\-\-image " PICTURE
A text on a dark background (default
.IR "Incident technique \- nous revenons dans un instant" ),
or a picture.
.TP
.BI \-\-duration " S"
Length (default 10 s), looped.
.TP
.B \-\-tone
1 kHz tone instead of silence.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on an error (configuration error, file not found, command refused); 2 on a usage
error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DVBTX_TOKEN
.B web.token
used by
.B dvbtx channel
to talk to a running transmitter.
.TP
.B HOME
UHD reads
.I ~/.config/uhd.conf
(FPGA image of a B210 clone...).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/dvbtx/dvbtx.toml
Configuration; other instances
.IR /etc/dvbtx/ NAME .toml
.RB ( dvbtx@ NAME .service ).
.TP
.I /usr/share/dvbtx/configs/
Example configurations.
.TP
.I /var/lib/dvbtx/
backup.ts, epg/ (EPG folder), gpu.json (transcoding ways learnt).
.TP
.I /run/dvbtx/
Work directory: engine.ini, SI tables.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/dvbtx/
dvbtx-engine, radio plugins dvbtx-sdr-*.so, the Python package.
.TP
.IR /usr/lib/systemd/system/dvbtx.service ", " dvbtx@.service ", " dvbtx\-power.service
systemd units.
.SH EXAMPLES
Validate a configuration, then transmit with it:
.PP
.EX
dvbtx check \-c /etc/dvbtx/dvbtx.toml
sudo dvbtx run \-c /etc/dvbtx/dvbtx.toml
.EE
.PP
No file: a pattern and a film on UHF channel 22 from a HackRF:
.PP
.EX
sudo dvbtx \-\-driver hackrf \-\-channel 22 \e
     \-\-service \(dqPattern=lavfi:testsrc2=size=1280x720:rate=25\(dq \e
     \-\-service \(dqMovie=/srv/videos/movie.mkv,lcn=2\(dq
.EE
.PP
Override settings of the file for one run:
.PP
.EX
sudo dvbtx run \-c my.toml \-s radio.0.gain=40 \-s carrier.1.frequency=498MHz
.EE
.PP
As a service:
.PP
.EX
sudo systemctl enable \-\-now dvbtx
sudo systemctl reload dvbtx          # EPG and channels of the file, live
journalctl \-u dvbtx \-f
.EE
.PP
Bit rates:
.PP
.EX
dvbtx calc dvbt \-\-table
dvbtx calc dvbt2 \-\-fft 32k \-\-extended yes \-\-constellation 256qam \-\-code\-rate 2/3
dvbtx calc dvbs2 \-\-symbol\-rate 27.5M \-\-modulation 8psk \-\-code\-rate 3/4
.EE
